<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan vegetable oil rates seen falling.</title>
<headline>Pakistan vegetable oil rates seen falling.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani vegetable oil prices are likely to fall next week on an expected higher production of sunflower oil and lower import of palm oil from abroad, dealers said on Saturday.</p>
<p>This week, RBD palm oil fell to $515 per tonne C&amp;F from $530 last week and soyoil remained unchanged at $555, a Saulat Enterprises dealer said. Vegoil stocks fell to 168,000 tonnes, including 110,000 tonnes of RBD palm oil and olein, from 180,000 last week.</p>
